Yes. Include a concise compliance statement that reflects your hospital’s policy and regulatory obligations, for example:

"This purchase complies with the hospital’s procurement and emergency expenditure policies, which allow authorized staff to obtain essential clinical supplies during shortages to ensure continuity and safety of patient care. I confirm that:
- All items purchased are standard, approved medical supplies used in this facility;
- No controlled substances were obtained outside of established protocols;
- The purchase was made solely for hospital use and not for personal benefit;
- I am requesting reimbursement in accordance with hospital policy and applicable health-care regulations, and I have attached all supporting documentation for audit review."

Adapt this wording so it matches your actual written policies and any specific language your compliance or risk-management office recommends.
